From c93c64efc2975f0737a6f57a858a253c8397e857 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:38:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(import): the STEP facet budget is a setting carried with
 the import

The STEP importer's facet budget (the constant MAX_FACETS) becomes a
value an import carries: ImportModel::within(path, budget), the script
verb cam.import(path, name?, facetBudget?) and MCP import_model's
optional facet_budget. The default is today's 30M cap, so no default
import changes; a budget outside 1000..=60000000, or one given for an
STL/OBJ file, is refused by name before parsing.

The budget a mesh was made under is recorded with the model
(schema::StepBudget, only when not the default) and traded with the
facets by import, update, repair, delete and their undo; the project
file keeps it as an optional facet_budget key (absent = default, so
older files load unchanged; out of bounds is refused at load). get_job
and cam.import report it. The reduced-fidelity flag is computed exactly
as before: a smaller budget flags, a larger one clears on re-import.
The refusal text now names the setting ("a larger STEP facet budget").

GUI: the model page carries a "STEP facet budget (next import)" row,
refused by name out of bounds, read by every STEP import the window
starts.

Fixes #1054

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
